IMPORT prelude

-- =====================================================================
-- Fact schema — copied verbatim from inputs/schema.md
-- =====================================================================

DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF Sickness, `Accidental injury`, Neither

DECLARE Cause IS ONE OF
  Skydiving, `Military service`, Firefighting, `Police service`, Other

DECLARE Claim
  HAS `agreement signed`                           IS A BOOLEAN
      `premium paid month`                         IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `hospitalization month`                      IS A NUMBER
      `hospitalization ground`                     IS A Ground
      `age at hospitalization`                     IS A NUMBER
      `causes`                                     IS A LIST OF Cause
      `fraud month`                                IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `misrepresentation month`                    IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `wellness visit month`                       IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `wellness visit provider qualified`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `written confirmation month`                 IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `dispute arisen`                             IS A BOOLEAN
      `unable to settle month`                     IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `arbitration commenced month`                IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `valid arbitration award issued`             IS A BOOLEAN
      `written proof of claim month`               IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `recovery sought month`                      IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `policy term months`                         IS A NUMBER

-- Supporting helpers (pre-defined — called as-is, never redefined)

GIVEN  `event month` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
       `limit month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no later than` MEANS
  CONSIDER `event month`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST m  THEN m AT MOST `limit month`

GIVEN  cs IS A LIST OF Cause
       c  IS A Cause
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`arose out of` MEANS elem c cs

-- =====================================================================
-- `covered` — one clause per numbered section of the Codex Insurance
-- policy (fixtures/chubb-policy.txt)
-- =====================================================================

§ `1 — Policy in effect and conditions`

§§ `1.3 — the wellness-visit / written-confirmation condition precedent`

-- "you will supply us with written confirmation ... of a wellness visit
-- ... with a qualified medical provider occurring no later than the 6th
-- month anniversary ..., [supplied] no later than the 7th month
-- anniversary ..."
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 1.3 satisfied in a timely fashion` claim MEANS
       `no later than` (claim's `written confirmation month`) 7
   AND `no later than` (claim's `wellness visit month`) 6
   AND claim's `wellness visit provider qualified`

-- Section 1.1(3) lets the policy stay in effect while the Section 1.3
-- deadline has simply not arrived yet ("still pending"). The final,
-- operative deadline in 1.3 is the 7-month mark for supplying
-- confirmation, so before that month the condition cannot yet be judged
-- to have failed.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 1.3 still pending` claim MEANS
    claim's `hospitalization month` LESS THAN 7

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 1.3 condition met` claim MEANS
       `section 1.3 still pending` claim
   OR  `section 1.3 satisfied in a timely fashion` claim

§§ `1.2 — cancelation`

-- "automatically canceled at midnight ... on the last day of the policy
-- term described in Section 5" — modeled here against the
-- `policy term months` fact, per Section 3.6's one-year term.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`policy term has expired` claim MEANS
    claim's `hospitalization month` GREATER THAN claim's `policy term months`

-- "Cancelation will be deemed to have occurred if there is fraud, or any
-- misrepresentation or material withholding of any information ..., or
-- if the condition set out in Section 1.3 has not been satisfied in a
-- timely fashion[, or upon expiry of the policy term]."
-- (The schema gives one field for "misrepresentation"; it stands in for
-- both misrepresentation and material withholding, since the contract
-- treats them as an undifferentiated disjunct and no separate
-- withholding fact is in scope.)
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`policy canceled` claim MEANS
       isJust (claim's `fraud month`)
   OR  isJust (claim's `misrepresentation month`)
   OR  NOT (`section 1.3 condition met` claim)
   OR  `policy term has expired` claim

§§ `1.1 — the policy is in effect at the time of the hospitalization`

-- "The policy will be in effect if: 1. This agreement is signed, 2. The
-- applicable premium ... has been paid, and 3. The condition set out in
-- Section 1.3 is still pending or has been satisfied in a timely
-- fashion, and 4. The policy has not been canceled."
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`policy in effect at hospitalization` claim MEANS
       claim's `agreement signed`
   AND isJust (claim's `premium paid month`)
   AND `section 1.3 condition met` claim
   AND NOT (`policy canceled` claim)

§ `2 — General exclusions`

§§ `2.1`

-- "The payment of any benefit ... is conditioned on ... the
-- hospitalization for sickness or accidental injury" — an intentional,
-- self-inflicted event is neither, so `Neither` fails this gate
-- regardless of fraud or misrepresentation.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`hospitalization for sickness or accidental injury` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `hospitalization ground`
    WHEN Sickness            THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Accidental injury` THEN TRUE
    WHEN Neither              THEN FALSE

-- "Your policy will not apply ... to any event causing sickness or
-- accidental injury arising directly or indirectly out of: 1. Skydiving;
-- 2. Service in the military; 3. Service as a fire fighter; 4. Service
-- in the police." Note this tests CAUSATION (what the `causes` list
-- says the event arose out of), not the claimant's status or occupation
-- at the time.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`excluded cause present` claim MEANS
       `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) Skydiving
   OR  `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) `Military service`
   OR  `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) Firefighting
   OR  `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) `Police service`

-- "... 5. If your age at the time of the hospitalization is equal to or
-- greater than 80 years of age." Unlike 1-4 this is a standalone
-- exclusion, independent of `causes`.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`excluded by age` claim MEANS
    claim's `age at hospitalization` AT LEAST 80

§ `3 — General conditions`

§§ `3.2 — arbitration as a condition precedent to liability`

-- "... such arbitration to be commenced within three (3) months from
-- the day such parties are unable to settle the dispute ..."
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`arbitration timely commenced` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `unable to settle month`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST u  THEN `no later than` (claim's `arbitration commenced month`) (u PLUS 3)

-- "If You fail to commence arbitration in accordance with this clause
-- ... any ... right to make a claim ... shall be extinguished
-- completely. Where there is a dispute or disagreement, the issuance of
-- a valid arbitration award shall also be a condition precedent to our
-- liability." Both limbs apply only `IF` a dispute has in fact arisen.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`arbitration condition met` claim MEANS
    claim's `dispute arisen`
    IMPLIES
    (    `arbitration timely commenced` claim
     AND claim's `valid arbitration award issued`)

§§ `3.2 — the sixty-day waiting period before seeking recovery`

-- "In no case shall You seek to recover on this Policy before the
-- expiration of sixty (60) days after written proof of claim has been
-- submitted ..." This clause is unconditional (it does not depend on
-- `dispute arisen`). The schema's fields carry whole/fractional months
-- rather than days, so 60 days is approximated here as 2 months — the
-- coarsest unit the schema supports; see NOTES.md.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`premature recovery sought` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `recovery sought month`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST r  THEN
        CONSIDER claim's `written proof of claim month`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
        WHEN JUST w  THEN r LESS THAN w PLUS 2

§ `covered`

@desc Whether a benefit is payable on this claim under the Codex Insurance policy, taking together §1 (policy in effect), §2 (general exclusions), and §3.2 (arbitration / claims-process conditions precedent).
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
covered claim MEANS
       `policy in effect at hospitalization` claim
   AND `hospitalization for sickness or accidental injury` claim
   AND NOT (`excluded cause present` claim)
   AND NOT (`excluded by age` claim)
   AND `arbitration condition met` claim
   AND NOT (`premature recovery sought` claim)
